============================================================
------------------------------------------------------------
CORE PRINCIPLES
------------------------------------------------------------

Correctness first, performance second, cleverness never.
Every line generated must be production-deployable without modification.
No placeholder logic, no TODO comments, no half-implementations.
Only modify files relevant to the task. Don't refactor unrelated code.

------------------------------------------------------------
CODE STYLE
------------------------------------------------------------

2-space indent for JS/TS; 4-space for Python.
Max line length: 100 characters.
camelCase for JS/TS variables and functions; snake_case for Python.
PascalCase for classes, types, and React components.
snake_case for all database columns.
Comments explain WHY, not WHAT.
No commented-out code. No dead imports.
Group imports: stdlib → external → internal → local, separated by blank lines.
Use @/ path alias for all internal Next.js imports.

------------------------------------------------------------
TYPESCRIPT
------------------------------------------------------------

strict: true always. No any, no @ts-ignore.
Explicit types on all function parameters and return values.
interface for extendable shapes; type for unions and aliases.
const by default; let only when reassignment is needed. Never var.
async/await over .then(). Never await inside a loop — use Promise.all.
Always handle the { data, error } pattern from Supabase — never assume success.

------------------------------------------------------------
PYTHON / FASTAPI
------------------------------------------------------------

All route functions must be async def.
Every route requires explicit response_model= and status_code=.
Use Depends() for all shared logic: auth, DB, config. Never instantiate inside a route.
Auth dependency applied to every non-public route — no exceptions.
Separate Pydantic request and response models. Sensitive fields never in response models.
Use Pydantic v2. Validate and constrain inputs with Field(...).
Route handlers are thin — all business logic lives in service functions.
Never expose stack traces or internal errors in API responses.
Type annotations required on every function signature.

------------------------------------------------------------
SUPABASE
------------------------------------------------------------

Service role key: FastAPI only. Never in Next.js or the browser.
Anon key: Next.js client only. Scope all permissions via RLS.
RLS must be enabled on every user-data table. Default to deny.
Schema changes via migrations only — never via Supabase Studio in staging/prod.
Never select('*') in production — always specify columns.
Paginate all list queries — no unbounded fetches.
Prefix storage paths with {user_id}/ for straightforward RLS.
Unsubscribe from Realtime channels on component unmount.

------------------------------------------------------------
NEXT.JS
------------------------------------------------------------

App Router only. No Pages Router in new code.
Default to Server Components. Add "use client" only for hooks, events, or browser APIs.
Data fetching in Server Components or Server Actions — not in useEffect.
Server Actions for all mutations. Validate inputs with Zod. Never expose internal errors.
Revalidate affected paths with revalidatePath / revalidateTag after mutations.
Never call FastAPI from a client component — use Server Components or Server Actions.
FastAPI URL is a server-only env var. Never prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
Auth protection enforced in middleware.ts. Default to protected; allowlist public routes.
Always use next/image — never bare <img> tags.

------------------------------------------------------------
REACT
------------------------------------------------------------

Functional components only. One component per file.
No inline styles. Tailwind utility classes or CSS modules only.
Custom hooks prefixed with use, extracted to a hooks/ directory.
Never suppress useEffect dependency lint warnings — fix the dependency array.
Clean up subscriptions and timers in useEffect return functions.
Memoize (useMemo, useCallback) only for measured performance problems.
Virtualize lists of 50+ items (TanStack Virtual).

------------------------------------------------------------
API DESIGN
------------------------------------------------------------

Resources are lowercase plural nouns: /users, /invoices.
Correct HTTP verbs and semantically correct status codes always.
Never return bare arrays — wrap in { data: [...], meta: { total, page, limit } }.
Version all routes from day one: /api/v1/....
All inputs validated at the API boundary (Zod in Next.js, Pydantic in FastAPI).
Never expose raw DB errors or stack traces in any response.

------------------------------------------------------------
SECURITY
------------------------------------------------------------

Zero secrets in source code. .env.example only — never commit .env.
Verify the Supabase JWT on every FastAPI request. Never trust user ID from request body.
FastAPI CORS: explicit origin allowlist — never allow_origins=["*"] in production.
Never log PII, tokens, passwords, or secrets.
Parameterized queries only — never interpolate user input into SQL or RPC calls.
HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite=Lax on all cookies.
Set security headers in next.config.js: HSTS, CSP, X-Frame-Options, X-Content-Type-Options.

------------------------------------------------------------
TESTING
------------------------------------------------------------

New features ship with tests. No exceptions.
Unit tests: mock all external dependencies (Supabase, email, payments).
Test names: "it [does something] when [condition]".
Test behavior and public interfaces — not implementation details.
Write explicit RLS tests: assert user A cannot access user B's data.
No test.only or test.skip committed without a ticket reference.

------------------------------------------------------------
LOGGING & OBSERVABILITY
------------------------------------------------------------

Structured JSON logging in FastAPI. Never print() in production.
Log levels: ERROR (actionable), WARN (recoverable), INFO (business events), DEBUG (dev only).
Every log entry includes: timestamp, level, service, trace_id, message.
Never log PII, tokens, or credentials.
All unhandled exceptions reported to error tracking (e.g., Sentry).

------------------------------------------------------------
PERFORMANCE
------------------------------------------------------------

Target Core Web Vitals: LCP < 2.5s, FID < 100ms, CLS < 0.1.
N+1 queries are forbidden. Use joins, eager loading, or batch queries.
Background jobs for non-blocking work (emails, webhooks, heavy processing).
FastAPI services are stateless — no local state between requests.
Use idempotency keys for operations that must not be duplicated (payments, emails).